# Scenario: two moles, one colony, left alone for a long time.
#
# This is the situation a fresh world actually produces. The spawn entry says
# minCount 1, maxCount 2, and NaturalSpawner offsets each group member by at
# most five blocks in x and z, so a pair standing together is the common case
# rather than an accident. What they then do to each other has never been
# watched.
#
# The questions it is here to answer:
#   - do two moles sharing one colony cooperate, or get in each other's way?
#   - does a colony ever reach NETWORK_MAX_MEMBERS, which is 32?
#   - and if it does, does the full-colony half of MoleEmigrateGoal fire? That
#     path needs `hasCompany` to find a second grown mole at home, which is
#     exactly what a pair provides and a lone mole never can. It has never run.

# 2048 chunks, x -512..511 and z -256..255. Bigger than the colony scenario
# because a dispersal aims COLONY_MIN_SEPARATION + EMIGRATION_MARGIN away - 272
# blocks - in whatever direction the bearing lands, and all of it has to be
# ticking or the run measures the edge of the square.
forceload add -512 -256 -257 -1
forceload add -256 -256 -1 -1
forceload add 0 -256 255 -1
forceload add 256 -256 511 -1
forceload add -512 0 -257 255
forceload add -256 0 -1 255
forceload add 0 0 255 255
forceload add 256 0 511 255

# Nothing may exist yet. Believe nothing below unless this says so.
say SOAK-CHECK empty-world
moleverse colony list

# Three blocks apart, which is what a spawn group looks like.
summon moleverse:mole 0 -2 0
summon moleverse:mole 3 -2 0

say SOAK-MARK setup-done

# Eight hours of game time, looked at every hour. A colony took two hours to
# reach twenty mounds with six moles spread over three colonies, so a pair
# working one colony needs the long form to have any chance of filling it.
tick sprint 72000
@wait Sprint completed
say SOAK-MARK hour-1
moleverse colony list
moleverse colony links

tick sprint 72000
@wait Sprint completed
say SOAK-MARK hour-2
moleverse colony links

tick sprint 72000
@wait Sprint completed
say SOAK-MARK hour-3
moleverse colony links

tick sprint 72000
@wait Sprint completed
say SOAK-MARK hour-4
moleverse colony links

tick sprint 72000
@wait Sprint completed
say SOAK-MARK hour-5
moleverse colony links

tick sprint 72000
@wait Sprint completed
say SOAK-MARK hour-6
moleverse colony links

tick sprint 72000
@wait Sprint completed
say SOAK-MARK hour-7
moleverse colony links

tick sprint 72000
@wait Sprint completed
say SOAK-MARK finished
moleverse colony list
moleverse colony links
